summary:
  A podcast feed healed to a new address no longer takes its alarm along,
  so "the newest episode of this show" searches a feed that stopped
  existing and the morning alarm rings silence.

history:
  The heal moved the subscription and the seen map and nothing else. The
  per-show speed, the downloads ledger's feed field and every alarm that
  named the show by its old address were left pointing at a feed nobody
  would ever fetch again (found 2026-09-05, fixed 2026-09-06). This mutant
  makes the alarm engine's retarget a silent no-op.

target:
  package/contents/ui/AlarmEngine.qml

find:
          if (!changed) return false;

replace:
          if (!changed || changed) return false;

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_alarmengine.qml
  test_a_healed_feed_moves_its_podcast_alarm. Line-neutral.
